title: Expository: James 2:14-17
description: James 2 written to saved Christians, to exercise our faith in the service of others; justified before men, not before God.
output: lessons/heresies/james-2-14-17.html

# From studies/data/notes/james-2-14-17-notes.html, in the author's words, arranged into slides.
# The notes quote James 2:18 in part; the slide shows the whole KJV verse with those words marked.

=== James 2
--- Expository: James 2:14-17 [title]
overline: Answering error
heading: Expository: James 2:14-17
sub: James 2 misunderstood
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

--- Can faith save him?
scripture: James 2:14-17 | mark: Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone

--- James 2 misunderstood
lead: James 2 misunderstood
p: Writing to saved Christians, to encourage those of us justified by the law of liberty ([[James 2:12]]), to exercise our faith in the service of others.
big: James 2:12 | mark: the law of liberty

--- What good is our faith?
lead: What good is our faith if we don’t also do for others?

--- Justified before men
lead: Justified before men
big: James 2:18 | mark: Thou hast faith, and I have works: shew me thy faith without thy works

=== Knowing this
--- Knowing this
p: Knowing this, that God so loved the world He gave His only begotten Son, that Jesus so loved the brethren that He gave His life for us that we may by faith receive the gift of eternal life, to be made sons of God and heirs to the Kingdom and the promises and blessings we have in this life and the next, sealed by the Spirit unto redemption…

--- The least we can do [title]
heading: The least we can do
lead: The least we can do in return is be a blessing to others. To show them the same love as Jesus showed us.
